  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "bs-04-reverse-equations-unknown-current",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Reverse Boat-and-Current Equations",
    "description": "Build one clean equation when a time difference, same-time condition, or measured leg hides the current.",
    "teachingApproach": "Start with a visible time-gap question and show how u+v and u−v turn words into one equation. Move through multiplicative time relations, same-time unequal distances, separate measured legs, and newer exam patterns that chain one recovered speed into another calculation.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 30,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 19, Boats and Streams. Approved scope: Teach learners to choose one unknown, express downstream and upstream speeds as u+v and u−v, and build an equation from time = distance/speed. Cover equal-distance time differences, upstream time being a multiple of downstream time, same-time unequal distances, deriving current from separate downstream/upstream journeys, solving still-water speed from a round-trip total with known current, and newer source patterns where a speed ratio or measured upstream rate is used to predict another distance or travel time."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn how to turn a river story into one useful equation.\n\nThe key is not to guess the current. Name it, build u + v and u − v, then translate the time condition exactly.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A boat moves at 10 mph in still water. It travels 36 miles each way. The upstream trip takes 1.5 hours longer than the downstream trip.\n\nLet current = v.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Then:\n36/(10−v) − 36/(10+v) = 1.5.\n\nFor v=2, the times are 36/8 = 4.5 h and 36/12 = 3 h.\nThe gap is 1.5 h, so v=2 mph.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
